{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Elohim called the dry land earth</b>. And this is what is mentioned in the first verse: ״בְּרֵאשִׁית״ etc. And the word <b>וַיִּקְרָא</b> may be explained in two ways: either in the sense of calling a name, or in the sense of crying out — He cried out against it so that it would not spread further, as they said, of blessed memory (Chagigah 12a), that He said to His world ״דַּי״ (enough), and since it heard and did not spread further, He called it ״אֶרֶץ,״ as they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 5:8), that it is called ״אֶרֶץ״ on account of its having been appeased (she-nitratzah)." "And His saying <b>He called the seas</b> — this is not the tehom mentioned in the second verse, for tehom refers to the totality of waters and those beneath the earth. Also, the gathered waters were then in the aspect of tehom before the earth appeared, for they were intermingled together with the waters that are today beneath the earth." "And His saying <b>and Elohim saw that it was good</b> refers back also to the gathering of the waters, for in this there is vitality and sustenance of the world, for from it come rains in the world, as they said, of blessed memory (Ta'anit 9b)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:54:59.785512776Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}